    "result_text": "All 269 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners, exposed as the integer `membershipNumber` field in the owner response. The acceptance test `Cp09Tests` reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the value must be persisted \u2014 I made it a real column, not a computed transient.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `Integer membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n3. **OpenAPI** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` (`integer`/`int32`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n4. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` sets `membershipNumber = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count), wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureUnique` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n\nThe value is assigned before the new owner is saved, so consecutive creations increment by exactly one, matching the spec and the Cp09 invariant. Full suite: **269 tests, 0 failures**.",
